$ Mo-Rh
$
$ TDB-file for the thermodynamic assessment of the Mo-Rh system
$
$-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ 2020.03.05
$ 
$ TDB file created by T.Abe, K.Hashimoto, and Y.Goto
$
$ Computational Structural Materials Design Group , National Institute for 
$ Materials Science. 1-2-1 Sengen, Tsukuba, Ibaraki 305-0047, Japan
$ e-mail: abe.taichi @nims.go.jp
$ Copyright (C) NIMS 2020
$
$-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ PARAMETERS ARE TAKEN FROM
$ A computer assessment of the molybdenum-rhodium phase diagram,
$ R.Gurler, J.N.Pratt, J.Alloys.Compd. 189 (1992) 97-100.
$
$-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ Comments
$ l. Lattice stability is very different from Unary 5.0 and is taken from 
$ S.A.Kats, V.Ya.Chekhovskoi, N.B.Gorina, V.Polyakova, E.M.Savitskii, 
$ V.S.E.S. 1. Konif, Kalorif, 2 (1977) 351-337. 
$
$ 2. The polynomial for the excess gibbs energy is differnt from R-K type
$ and thus was converted in this TDB.
$
$ 3. Calculated phase diagram and gibbs energy of the pahse are slightly 
$ different from given figures. 
$
$                                                                  T.A.
$-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 ELEMENT /-   ELECTRON_GAS              0.0000E+00  0.0000E+00  0.0000E+00 !
 ELEMENT VA   VACUUM                    0.0000E+00  0.0000E+00  0.0000E+00 !
 ELEMENT MO   BCC_A2                    9.5940E+01  4.5890E+03  2.8560E+01 !
 ELEMENT RH   FCC_A1                    1.0291E+02  4.9204E+03  3.1505E+01 !
$
$-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 TYPE_DEFINITION % SEQ *!
 DEFINE_SYSTEM_DEFAULT SPECIE 2 !
 DEFAULT_COMMAND DEF_SYS_ELEMENT VA /- !

$-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ MO
$-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 FUNCTION GHSERMO  298.15  +0;                                     6000 N !
 FUNCTION GLIQMO   298.15  +41402.91-14.2966*T+GHSERMO;            6000 N !
 FUNCTION GFCCMO   298.15  +15200+0.63*T+GHSERMO;                  6000 N ! 
 FUNCTION GHCPMO   298.15  +11550+GHSERMO;                         6000 N !

$-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ RH
$-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  FUNCTION GHSERRH  298.15  +0;                                    6000 N !
  FUNCTION GLIQRH   298.15  +26568.0-11.88*T+GHSERRH ;             6000 N !
  FUNCTION GBCCRH   298.15  +6904+4.39*T+GHSERRH;                  6000 N !
  FUNCTION GHCPRH   298.15  +628+0.63*T+GHSERRH;                   6000 N !

$-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ LIQUID
$-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 PHASE  LIQUID % 1 1     !
   CONSTITUENT  LIQUID : MO,RH    :   !
  PARAMETER G(LIQUID,MO;0)    298.15  +GLIQMO;                     6000 N !
  PARAMETER G(LIQUID,RH;0)    298.15  +GLIQRH;                     6000 N !
  PARAMETER G(LIQUID,MO,RH;0) 298.15  -102595.3+40.525*T;          6000 N !
  PARAMETER G(LIQUID,MO,RH;1) 298.15  +42341.205-22.19*T;          6000 N !
  PARAMETER G(LIQUID,MO,RH;2) 298.15  -6.945+0.055*T;              6000 N !

$-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ BCC_A2
$-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 PHASE  BCC % 1 1     !
   CONSTITUENT  BCC : MO,RH :   !
  PARAMETER G(BCC,MO;0)    298.15  +GHSERMO;                    6000 N !
  PARAMETER G(BCC,RH;0)    298.15  +GBCCRH;                     6000 N !
  PARAMETER G(BCC,MO,RH;0) 298.15  +1618.97-9.315*T;            6000 N !
  PARAMETER G(BCC,MO,RH;1) 298.15  +20888.46+3.835*T;           6000 N !

$-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ FCC_A1
$-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 PHASE FCC % 1 1 !
   CONSTITUENT  FCC : MO,RH :   !
  PARAMETER G(FCC,MO;0)    298.15  +GFCCMO;                     6000 N !
  PARAMETER G(FCC,RH;0)    298.15  +GHSERRH;                    6000 N !
  PARAMETER G(FCC,MO,RH;0) 298.15  +10412.809-15.294*T;         6000 N !
  PARAMETER G(FCC,MO,RH;1) 298.15  +99700.75-49.71*T;           6000 N !

$-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ HCP_A3
$-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 PHASE  HCP %  1 1     !
   CONSTITUENT  HCP : MO,RH :   !
  PARAMETER G(HCP,MO;0)    298.15  +GHCPMO;                     6000 N !
  PARAMETER G(HCP,RH;0)    298.15  +GHCPRH;                     6000 N !
  PARAMETER G(HCP,MO,RH;0) 298.15  -38456.402+7.441*T;          6000 N !
  PARAMETER G(HCP,MO,RH;1) 298.15  +30003.25-12.936*T;          6000 N !

$--------------------------------------------------------------------END OF LINE